
  Moggie -- open firmware for the Sonos Play:5 Gen 1
  =================================================

  Console access is a root shell with no password prompt. That is
  deliberate: the UART is inside the case, and root's password in
  /etc/shadow is locked, so no password can authenticate anything.

  SSH is off unless you provision, on the jffs2 partition (mtd1):

      /jffs/ssh/enable           (any content)
      /jffs/ssh/host_key         dropbear host key
      /jffs/ssh/authorized_keys  your public key(s)

  Dropbear then runs with password authentication disabled.

  Settings live in /jffs/sonosd.conf (symlinked from /etc/sonosd.conf).
  Logs: /var/log/sonosd.log (tmpfs, lost on reboot).

